        Rating: 1,
        Description:
          "Misleading photos and disappointing stay\n\nAs an American traveler who has stayed in hotels across both Africa and India—including some at much lower rates—I can honestly say this was one of my most disappointing hotel experiences.\n\nMisleading presentation:\nThe photos online were deceiving—either very old or heavily edited. The room we were given smelled terrible. The furniture, especially the chairs and cabinets, had a strong urine odor, and the overall space smelled damp and moldy. The bedding felt moist and unclean, and there was visible water warping on the floor and bathroom door, which made it difficult to open and close.\n\nRoom and maintenance issues:\nWe initially tried to overlook these problems since we were happy to have a Western toilet and overhead shower, but on the first day, our shower caused the entire bathroom to flood. I had to unplug the hair dryer out of fear of electrocution. When we called for help, the staff discovered the drain was clogged with a thick buildup of hair—clearly not cleaned between guests. On top of that, the drain wasn’t even installed at the low point, so water couldn’t flow out properly.\n\nAlthough staff came promptly, they used a bath towel to mop up the dirty water—without any disinfectant—dragging it across the floor. Later, we realized our refrigerator had not been running while we were out, since power shuts off when you remove the keycard. We had food stored inside, and my husband later became ill. We strongly suspect it was due to the fridge not staying on, which feels like a cost-cutting measure on the hotel’s part.\n\nFrom that point on, we wore our shoes inside because the floor no longer felt clean.\n\nSanitation and plumbing problems:\nTwo days later, dirty toilet water began seeping from around the base of the toilet. The staff initially dismissed it, took a long coffee break, and only later came to address the issue. Again, the floor was “cleaned” with a bath towel and no disinfectant. Every time we requested clean towels, we only received part of what we asked for.\n\nThe soap provided was from a push-style dispenser attached to the wall, filled with low-quality liquid soap that felt diluted and had an unpleasant scent.\n\nRoom change:\nAfter repeated complaints, we were finally moved to a much nicer room—but by then, the frustration had overshadowed the gesture.\n\nOther observations:\nThe elevator (lift) was also malfunctioning during our stay. I understand that the building is older, but proper upkeep and small improvements could easily maintain its quality and justify its rating.\n\nWe didn’t try the hotel restaurant due to multiple reviews mentioning food poisoning. Another couple in our group did eat there; while they didn’t get sick, they said the menu was limited.\n\nPositives:\nThe Blue Tokai coffee shop downstairs was excellent—great service and quality coffee. The security guards were also very kind and professional. The neighborhood felt safe, though the hotel’s location is quite far from most Delhi attractions.\n\nOverall:\nFor the price, the value did not align at all. The hotel’s appearance online does not match reality, and the lack of basic cleanliness, maintenance, and hygiene standards makes it impossible for me to recommend—especially at its current rate.",
